From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kylechar <kylechar@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 16:20:04 -0800
Subject: Treat recorderer snap() failure as a failure

GraphiteFlush() was treating recorder->snap() returning null as
success, even thoguh it only returns null for an error. Treat it as a
failure to flush instead.

Fixed: 574795295
Change-Id: I1fc9363c26c92884273240a9f3d952bb21a5c547
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8717309
Reviewed-by: Greg Daniel <egdaniel@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Michael Ludwig <michaelludwig@google.com>
Commit-Queue: Kyle Charbonneau <kylechar@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1737029}

diff --git a/gpu/command_buffer/service/graphite_utils.cc b/gpu/command_buffer/service/graphite_utils.cc
index 9dd217e037cf950525786fb1b68a956e2de3ccd8..43b9f47f4195b127e882be0c883c84ff13a179cd 100644
--- a/gpu/command_buffer/service/graphite_utils.cc
+++ b/gpu/command_buffer/service/graphite_utils.cc
@@ -71,7 +71,8 @@ bool GraphiteFlush(GraphiteSharedContext* context,
   if (recording) {
     return context->insertRecording({recording.get()});
   }
-  return true;
+  // Snap will only return null if there is an error.
+  return false;
 }
 
 bool GraphiteFlushAndSubmit(GraphiteSharedContext* context,
